{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-207405-r4514125","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Thai Shrimp","sourcePageId":207405,"sourceRevision":"4514125","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:43:07Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Thai%20Shrimp&oldid=4514125","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:16.807Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock","Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles","Category:Recipes using peanut oil","Category:Recipes using red bell pepper","Category:Recipes using shrimp","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Thai recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"8b1d986fa86df117489ffae1b2ac78211e7d1180560d0afa6e869664417b81e5","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Seafood recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} \n\n== Ingredients ==\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Thai Chili Paste|Thai chili paste]]\n* 2 tbsp rice [[Cookbook:Wine vinegar|wine vinegar]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Sesame Oil|sesame oil]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Chicken Broth|chicken broth]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Peanut Oil|peanut oil]]\n* 24 jumbo [[Cookbook:Shrimp|shrimp]], peeled and deveined\n* ¼ red [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], [[Cookbook:Julienne|julienned]]\n* ¼ green bell pepper, julienned\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* Salt, to taste\n* Pepper, to taste\n* 1 tbsp toasted [[Cookbook:Sesame Seed|sesame seeds]]\n* Hot cooked rice or noodles (optional)\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine soy sauce, chili paste, vinegar, sugar, cornstarch, sesame oil and broth. Set aside.\n#Preheat a large [[Cookbook:Sauté Pan|sauté pan]] or [[Cookbook:Wok|wok]] over high heat. Add peanut oil and shrimp and [[Cookbook:Stir-frying|stir-fry]] until shrimp is pink. Remove and keep warm.\n#Add bell pepper and garlic and stir-fry until bell pepper has taken on slight browning. Remove and keep warm.\n#Add liquid mixture to pan and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. Cook until liquid has reduced to ¼ cup.\n#Add shrimp and vegetables back to pan and [[Cookbook:Mixing#Tossing|toss]]. Heat through.\n#Garnish with sesame seeds and serve immediately over rice or noodles.  \n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* If you're serving this to somebody with a peanut allergy, don't be worried. The allergens are in the protein part, not the fat part. However, steer clear of these peanut oils: Cold press and organic, which we wouldn't use anyways, because they have too low of a smoke point.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp]]\n[[Category:Thai recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell peppe